## Failure and rollback

- Preserve the first concrete error before restarting or retrying.
- Stop when prerequisites, scope, or project identity are ambiguous.
- Use the smallest rollback that restores the last verified state.
- Never force-push, delete user data, expose credentials, or change production topology without explicit approval.

## Recipe memory

Save only redacted, replayable steps. Never persist file bodies, tokens, cookies, auth URLs, or secret-bearing command arguments. A failed run is evidence but must not replace a successful recipe.
